<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/clipboard-inspection.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/clipboard-inspection-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/clipboard-inspection.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/free-claim-calculators/">Calculators</a></li><li aria-current="page">Claim Timeline Planner</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Free planner</p><h1>Washington Property Claim Timeline Planner</h1><p class="lede">Policy deadlines keep running while you argue about a number. Enter your date of loss and your policy’s windows to build a timeline you can add to your calendar.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="tool" data-tool="dates">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim timeline planner</span><i>Exports to your calendar</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div><label for="t-d">Date of loss</label><input id="t-d" type="date" name="dol"></div>
      <p class="hint flush">Adjust each window to match your policy. Defaults are common figures, not legal advice.</p>
      <div class="days-grid">
        <div><label for="t-n">Report claim within (days)</label><input id="t-n" name="notice" inputmode="numeric" value="3"></div>
        <div><label for="t-m">Temporary repairs within (days)</label><input id="t-m" name="mitig" inputmode="numeric" value="10"></div>
        <div><label for="t-p">Proof of loss (days)</label><input id="t-p" name="pol" inputmode="numeric" value="60"><span class="hint">Often counted from the insurer’s request.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-r">Depreciation recovery (days)</label><input id="t-r" name="rcd" inputmode="numeric" value="180"></div>
        <div><label for="t-s">Suit limitation (days)</label><input id="t-s" name="suit" inputmode="numeric" value="365"><span class="hint">Many Washington homeowner policies use one year.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <ol class="timeline" data-o="timeline"></ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn small" data-ics>Download .ics calendar file</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you enter is stored.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The deadlines that matter most</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Prompt notice.</strong> Policies require you to report losses promptly. Late notice is a common defense.</li>
<li><strong>Proof of loss.</strong> If the insurer asks for a sworn proof of loss, many policies give 60 days to send it.</li>
<li><strong>Depreciation recovery.</strong> Replacement cost policies often require repairs within a set period to collect holdback.</li>
<li><strong>Suit limitation.</strong> Washington law doesn’t allow policies to set less than one year to sue, and many homeowner policies use exactly one year. Appraisal may not pause that clock.</li></ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Important</b>This planner uses the numbers you enter. It isn’t legal advice, and courts can read policy deadlines differently. If a deadline is close, contact a Washington attorney.</div>
<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the date of loss the day I noticed the damage?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually it’s the date of the storm or event. Weather records for your address can help pin it down.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does demanding appraisal extend my suit deadline?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not automatically. Some policies or written agreements address it, but many don’t. Protect the deadline separately.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free calculators</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/free-claim-calculators/appraisal-readiness-quiz/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Free checklist</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Appraisal Readiness Quiz</h3><span class="pcard-p">Answer 12 yes-or-no questions to score your claim file and get a to-do list before you demand appraisal.</span><span class="pcard-more">Open <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/free-claim-calculators/wildfire-total-loss-coverage-check/"><s